      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "BTS — FAKE LOVE",
      "content": "Something done completely, often with \"dammit, it happened.\"\n\nThe title track from Love Yourself: Tear (2018), the album that pushed BTS's 'Love Yourself' series toward its darkest point. The whole Love Yourself arc is about learning to love yourself before you can love anyone else — and FAKE LOVE is the moment that lesson gets learned the hard way.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn the grammar pattern **-아/어 버리다**, which means \"to do completely / with finality.\" We'll see how BTS uses it in \"FAKE LOVE.\"",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "이번에 배울 것",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서 배울 단어:\n- **지우다** — to erase\n- **떠나다** — to leave\n- **잊어 버리다** — to completely forget\n- **떠나 버리다** — to leave for good\n\n레슨이 끝나면, 이 노래의 가사를 이해할 수 있어요.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
